<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
	<ThingDef ParentName="ApparelBase" Name="LithicApparelBase" Abstract="True">
		<techLevel>Neolithic</techLevel>
		<smeltable>false</smeltable>
		<tickerType>Normal</tickerType>
		<tradeTags>
			<li>ET_LithicArmorTag</li>
		</tradeTags>
	</ThingDef>

<!--TO-DO: LITHIC MANTLE

MANTLE WILL HAVE 2 STAGES ON LAUNCH

	-BASE STAGE: WILL INCLUDE "FORTIFY" ABILITY
	-SECOND STAGE STAGE: WILL INCLUDE "SHOCK BURST" ABILITY
	-THIRD STAGE: WILL INCLUDE "LIGHTNING BOLT" ABILITY

ARMOR ABILITIES:
	FORTIFY: INCREASES DEFENSES FOR A COUPLE HOURS BUT DECREASES MOVEMENT, ETC. FOR THE SAMER ABOUTN OF TIME
	SHOCK BURST: FIRES A BURST OF ELECTRICITY THAT SHOCKS A TARGETS IN A SMALL AREA. DAMAGE + CHANCE TO EMP
	LIGHTNING BOLT: FIRES A DIRECTED BOLT OF LIGHTNING AT A TARGET. MEDIUM RANGE, MEDIUM DAMAGE


ANOTHER ARMOR WILL INCLUDE THE FOURTH STAGE:
	STORM BARRAGE: FIRES 5 QUICK BLASTS OF ELECTRIC DAMAGE ON A TARGET. 
-->

	<ThingDef ParentName="LithicApparelBase">
		<defName>ET_LithicLightArmorT1_Base</defName>
		<label>genesite nomad armor</label>
		<techLevel>Neolithic</techLevel>
		<description>An armor made entirely of genesite, far different from any stone that can normally be found. Genesite only exists near the core of a planet, making it impossible to acquire with traditional mining methods.
This particular set of armor - which is more akin to a protective working suit - was made with efficiency in mind, layering *just* enough of the stone to provide protection, while also not being heavy or imposing movement restrictions.
The offered mobility and durability made it especially ideal for terratechists that chose to wander the planet instead of settling down, giving the armor it's name.
This specific set can be charged with Shocksap, which will cause special crystals to grow. These crystals provide electrical abilities to the wearer; however the crystals also replace the genesite material, diminishing the armor's defensive capabilities.</description>
		<graphicData>
			<texPath>Things/Apparel/LithicLightArmorT1Base/LithicLightArmorT1Base</texPath>
			<graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
			<drawSize>1</drawSize>
		</graphicData>
		<generateCommonality>0</generateCommonality>
		<statBases>
			<Mass>4.6</Mass>
			<MaxHitPoints>600</MaxHitPoints>			<!--Durability is 60% of base, rounded up to nearest 5th)-->
			<MarketValue>200</MarketValue>
			<DeteriorationRate>0</DeteriorationRate>
			<Flammability>0</Flammability>
			<ArmorRating_Sharp>0.2</ArmorRating_Sharp>
			<ArmorRating_Blunt>0.25</ArmorRating_Blunt>
			<ArmorRating_Heat>0.15</ArmorRating_Heat>
			<Insulation_Cold>2</Insulation_Cold>
			<Insulation_Heat>5</Insulation_Heat>
			<EquipDelay>14</EquipDelay>
		</statBases>
		<thingCategories>
			<li>ApparelArmor</li>
		</thingCategories>
		<equippedStatOffsets>
			<MoveSpeed>-0.1</MoveSpeed>
			<IncomingDamageFactor>-0.1</IncomingDamageFactor>
		</equippedStatOffsets>
		<apparel>
			<tags>
				<li>LithicArmor</li>
			</tags>
			<wornGraphicPath>Things/Apparel/LithicLightArmorT1Base/LithicLightArmorT1Base</wornGraphicPath>
			<layers>
				<li>OnSkin</li>
				<li>Middle</li>
				<li>Shell</li>
			</layers>
			<bodyPartGroups>
				<li>Torso</li>
				<li>Neck</li>
				<li>Shoulders</li>
				<li>Arms</li>
				<li>Legs</li>
				<li>Feet</li>
				<li>Waist</li>
			</bodyPartGroups>
			<defaultOutfitTags>
				<li>Soldier</li>
			</defaultOutfitTags>
			<drawData>

			</drawData>
		</apparel>
		<comps>
			<li Class="CompProperties_InspectString">
				<inspectString>&lt;color=#BD9ABB&gt;Lithic-class&lt;/color&gt; | &lt;color=#D46F44&gt;Stage I&lt;/color&gt;
-10% damage taken | Ability: Fortify | ???</inspectString>
			</li>
		</comps>
	</ThingDef>

	<ThingDef ParentName="LithicApparelBase">
		<defName>ET_LithicLightArmorT1Helmet_Base</defName>
